# Demonstrates the "nuke and re-prompt" eviction design: try_auto_early_
# wake() silently adopting an early-wake slot for a newly-conflicted timer
# B deliberately evicts a DIFFERENT, still-running timer A's earlier
# accepted plan (the single shared early-wake slot is unconditionally
# overwritten) - and then confirms A gets a fresh, working conflict check
# of its own once it becomes the priority target again, rather than
# silently never being revisited (see try_auto_early_wake's own "NOT A
# BUG" comment block and the wakeup_conflict_remaining_sites memory notes
# for the full reasoning/invariant this relies on).
#
# Since acceptance is now fully silent/automatic, this walkthrough can't
# directly observe the eviction moment (no window, no log/persisted-
# storage assertions - v1 framework limitation, see
# tests/functional_framework/README.md's "What this v1 does not do") -
# only prove A wasn't silently abandoned via the final re-prompt step.
#
# NOTE: live-verified (2026-09-30) - TestSetTimerRemainingDisplay values
# are measured from a live run, not guessed; re-verify if this file's
# button sequence changes.
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq

# Timer A (id 1, 300s) - seeded and started first, becomes the initial
# target (rearm_wakeup() always evaluates the GLOBALLY soonest running
# timer via tc_soonest_end()/find_soonest_unarmed_running_idx() - it does
# NOT matter which timer's TestSetTimerIndex was just touched). Only its own
# exact minute is blocked (offset 0 relative to whichever timer is
# currently being evaluated - see wakeup_conflict_basic_resolutions.seq
# for why Pos offset 0 alone doesn't actually constrain wakeup_find_
# early_slot()'s backward search), leaving room elsewhere -
# try_auto_early_wake() silently finds and adopts a slot for it.
# Live-verified (2026-09-27, native emulator + APP_LOG instrumentation)
# with 300s/150s durations - see below for why B must be strictly SHORTER
# than A, not merely a different value.
# Screenshots below each send a TestSetTimerRemainingDisplay(+tolerance)
# per still-running timer (A=idx0, B=idx1) - values are measured from a
# live run (each timer's own backdoor value minus real elapsed seconds
# observed at that checkpoint), not the raw backdoor value, with a small
# tolerance for run-to-run variance. Only one TestSetTimerIndex fits per
# AppMessage, so A and B each get their own APPMSG line.
APPMSG --string 10027="0"
APPMSG --string 10000="$(printf 'Timer A\037300\0371')"
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10021=1 10022=300
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10029=296 10030=8 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
SCREENSHOT a_silently_resolved

# Timer B (id 2, 150s) - seeded and started AFTER A, with a SHORTER
# duration than A's remaining - this is the one thing that actually makes
# B (not A) the new global-soonest target from this point on, since
# rearm_wakeup()'s target is always whichever running timer's end_time is
# earliest overall, not whichever timer a message happened to touch. (An
# earlier draft of this test gave A and B equal durations, on the mistaken
# assumption that "started later" alone was enough to make B the target -
# live-verified false: with equal durations A, started first, keeps the
# earlier end_time and stays the target forever, so B's own conflict path
# is never even exercised and nothing is ever evicted.) Duration is
# moderate (150s, not the original 60s) so there's enough backward room in
# wakeup_find_early_slot() for the still-irrelevant offset-0 block to
# succeed immediately as expected - at 60s there's almost no room before
# the `candidate <= time(NULL)` cutoff, and try_auto_early_wake() can fail
# outright regardless of blocking. B's own try_auto_early_wake() finds a
# slot and unconditionally evicts A's earlier accepted plan. Still no
# window.
APPMSG --string 10000="$(printf 'Timer A\037300\0371\036Timer B\037150\0372')"
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=1 10021=1 10022=150
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10029=284 10030=8 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
APPMSG --int 10020=1 10029=144 10030=8 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
SCREENSHOT b_silently_resolved_evicted_a

# Widen the block to offsets 0-7 (using the full TEST_BLOCKED_MINUTES_MAX=8
# budget) - safe to send now even though B is still the current target,
# since B's already-accepted plan shields it via rearm_wakeup()'s
# early-wake-covered fast path (no re-test happens as long as the plan's
# owner is still the target).
APPMSG --string 10028="0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7"
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10029=273 10030=10 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
APPMSG --int 10020=1 10029=133 10030=8 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
SCREENSHOT b_still_fine_after_widened_block

# Take B out of the running pool - A becomes the global-soonest target
# again (the only running timer left). TestSetTimerIndex's own handler calls
# abandon_early_wake_if_for() on the timer it's stopping BEFORE its
# rearm_wakeup() call, so B's accepted plan (and the early_wake_timer_id
# bookkeeping pointing at it) is explicitly retired here, not left
# dangling - then the same handler's routing through handle_wakeup_
# result() re-triggers a fresh check for whichever timer is now globally
# soonest (A). Since A's own earlier plan was evicted by B back when B
# adopted its slot, and A's remaining duration by now is short enough that
# only a few backward candidates exist before wakeup_find_early_slot()'s
# `candidate <= time(NULL)` cutoff, the offsets-0-7 block above exhausts
# all of them. This should genuinely fail and open a FRESH conflict window
# for A, proving it wasn't silently abandoned when its plan was evicted.
APPMSG --int 10020=1 10021=0
SLEEP 1
# B is now idle (its shown value, if any, is always its real
# time-independent t->remaining regardless of override - see
# run_control_pause_resume_stop.seq's comment on this), so only A gets an
# override here.
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10029=262 10030=10 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
SCREENSHOT a_gets_fresh_reprompt
# Expect: the single-row "Ok" informational window, naming Timer A.

# Clean up: acknowledge it.
TAP select
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10020=0 10029=253 10030=10 10033=0 --string 10031="12:00"
SCREENSHOT final_state
